<title>UK: Kvaerner gets UK support for China bridge.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner gets UK support for China bridge.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Norwegian engineering group Kvaerner ASA said on Tuesday it received financial backing for a contract won by its Cleveland Bridge Ltd unit to build the Jiangyin suspension bridge near Nanjing in China.</p>
<p>The company said Britain's official export credit agency, the Export Credits Guarantee Department (ECGD), was guaranteeing a $89.3 million loan arranged by BZW, part of Barclays Plc, to China Construction Bank to help finance the contract.</p>
<p>The bridge, to be built over the Yangtse River and opened in 1999, will be one of the longest in the world, according to the company.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
